==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 6.67~16 seconds<sup>200f~480f</sup>.
*6 [[Gory Dark]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 40~80 seconds<sup>1,200f~2,400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 0.67~6 seconds<sup>20f~180f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Fireworks Guys (High-Yield)]] spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 50~50.67 seconds<sup>1,500f~1,520f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Fireworks Guys (Low-Yield)]] spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 40~40.67 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,220f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Dark Emperor Nyandam]] spawns as the boss.
**2 [[Gory Dark]]s spawn, delay 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Shy Boy]]s spawn, delay 20~40 seconds<sup>600f~1,200f</sup>.
**1 [[The Face]] spawns.

==Strategy==
If you have any units that outrange Nyandam, definitely bring them. The Face does not pose a threat because of its average range and attack rate. If you do not have a unit that outranges Nyandam, then you can rush it down with units like A. Bahamut. You can time the Cat Cannon to reset his attack animation to rush him down. The Shy Boys provide plenty of cash, so another option is simply spam all your units and eventually take down Nyandam.

